8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9794ff52d6ad7cd08e96633e465f565d1e9012587ab2beac09788dc1f7e56506","event_uuid":"50c9daf1-5c5b-43ac-95ec-8cf1450c1a21","position":{"commit_sha":"b1250a1a63ad1f72b206e70c1a8e940e2de76006","position":"1785775778402039001-50c9daf1-5c5b-43ac-95ec-8cf1450c1a21"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b6ca6901e78bfbc6aabbe712f3d12c7ded5f8ad7d673b1a70c60241e949e5728","event_uuid":"43e10781-9b7a-451a-ba8f-9108ae365328","position":{"commit_sha":"2bf8d623599f1b38ea10f930282280182de4432a","position":"1785775780323464001-43e10781-9b7a-451a-ba8f-9108ae365328"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Remediated BLOCK findings E4/G6 and advisory E6. Recorded A4-1 landed evidence (Gerrit 1256, commit 6cdd4b00d9ee, both votes +1), corrected the stale downstream-savings premise, pinned the exact empty-local-fields gate with a worked example, and anchored the git counter at exactly zero with a positive control. The parent already carries the A4-2 dependency; rebar correctly rejected duplicating a depends_on edge from the child to the closed ticket.","timestamp":1785774000103053001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"A4-3 no-change verification completed on origin/main b263218542. A4-1 landed evidence: Gerrit 1256 / commit 6cdd4b00d9ee, LLM-Review +1, Verified +1. Raw-vs-production filter plus positive controls: 3/3 passed (test_key_set_prev_field_drift_never_survives_the_production_filter, test_a_genuinely_new_remote_key_still_plans_its_inbound_create, test_seed_mutations_survive_the_suppression). Convergence controls: 3/3 passed (unchanged remote idempotency, byte/HEAD preservation, real remote field change converges). Live counter probe: positive_control=1, then empty production batch snapshot_head calls=0 and manifest mutation_count=0. Corpus: 4/4 real snapshot pairs, forward non-empty effect differences=0, reverse differences=0, unexpected inbound creates=0, max key-set bytes=16,297. The first parallel integration invocation passed its test body but teardown caught concurrent pytest cache creation; serial rerun with cacheprovider disabled passed cleanly. No source/test/docs files changed. Operator attestation: the proposed differ edit is intentionally not made because A4-1 load-bearing source/tests require suppression at the exceptional snapshot call site.","timestamp":1785775316048354001}],"created_at":1785730141297716001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Resolution discovered during plan review\n\nNo production change is warranted. A4-1 already solved the operational defect at the correct boundary and deliberately preserved the raw differ contract.\n\nThe raw `compute_mutations(local_state, jira_state)` API must treat its first argument as real local state. For `local_state = {\"RB-8\": {}}` and `jira_state = {\"RB-8\": {\"summary\": \"remote\"}}`, it emits a `field_drift` update. That behavior is a load-bearing positive control for callers that honor the API contract.\n\nThe sole production snapshot caller does not honor that contract: it passes `prev_snapshot` and `curr_snapshot`, both remote Jira state. A4-1, merged as Gerrit 1256 / `6cdd4b00d9ee` with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, filters differ-owned `field_drift` and `unbound_local` emissions immediately at that call site. The source and tests explicitly require the filter to remain there so a future migration to real local state can remove it without weakening the pure differ.\n\nChanging `_compute_mutations_emit_both` as originally proposed would contradict that decision and break the raw-differ positive control. This ticket therefore verifies the already-landed behavior and records the no-change decision.\n\n## Verification plan\n\n- Run `test_key_set_prev_field_drift_never_survives_the_production_filter`; it proves the raw positive control emits and the production call-site result contains zero outbound updates.\n- Run `test_a_genuinely_new_remote_key_still_plans_its_inbound_create` and `test_seed_mutations_survive_the_suppression`; they prove the filter does not swallow genuine work or invariant repairs.\n- Run the converged `reconcile_once` and real-repository idempotency tests; they prove persisted `mutation_count == 0`.\n- Execute an in-session counting probe around the real production path with a key-set previous snapshot. Prove the counter observes a representative `git rev-parse` call in its positive control, then assert zero per-mutation calls after the A4-1 filter.\n- Record exact commands and outcomes on this ticket and the epic session log. No source, test, or documentation file is changed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] [code-verifiable] The raw differ emits its documented field-drift positive control while the production snapshot call-site result contains zero outbound updates for the same key-set entry.\n- [x] [code-verifiable] Genuine inbound-create and invariant-seed mutations survive the call-site filter.\n- [x] [code-verifiable] A converged pass records `mutation_count == 0`.\n- [x] [code-verifiable] An instrumented production-path probe records exactly zero per-mutation `git rev-parse` calls and its positive control proves the counter is live.\n- [x] [operator-attested] The no-change decision, A4-1 Gerrit evidence, commands, and results are recorded on this ticket.\n\n## File impact\n\nNone. A4-1 already contains the production filter and load-bearing characterization tests.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","4804-d9eb-e682-4d9c"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"A4-1 already landed the production call-site suppression and its load-bearing characterization; this ticket verifies and records the no-change decision.","parent_id":"4804-d9eb-e682-4d9c","parent_status_uuid":"50c9daf1-5c5b-43ac-95ec-8cf1450c1a21","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["bridge-state","reconciler","diffing"],"ticket_id":"bf03-73bf-b66a-4c84","ticket_type":"task","title":"A4-3 verification: accept A4-1 call-site suppression and make no differ change","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["645886d8-d552-4d1b-8813-a636bf8aace9","6263b4db-3d9f-40d9-874f-13b9fb640f5f","b2d14b1f-3d6e-4e4a-8764-aaefb71829ec","b49d50da-b8d7-49f7-bcc7-bf1400fa998c","7b381975-d927-45fb-a2f6-78f964e6019d","59344156-6698-4df3-8252-4a9fe1b1da12","f0614d06-238f-4e90-ba77-edb777e05f79","018aeb1e-8900-4ede-b211-7854d91d0e9b","507c42dc-896f-40ca-9471-bd7743761b48","250606f0-06e9-4ec8-9a03-69c37d1f4faa","50c9daf1-5c5b-43ac-95ec-8cf1450c1a21","43e10781-9b7a-451a-ba8f-9108ae365328"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659658344382001,"uuid":"65a67337-2376-451b-9070-4a28e65582dd"}